# Python concepts & interview study

Use this rule when the user asks to learn, document, or practice Python concepts, data structures, tricky language questions, or common interview / LeetCode-style problems.

## Preferred example domain

When the user does not provide a domain, prefer examples from an **online computer shopping management system**:

- hardware: laptop, mouse, keyboard, monitor, printer, storage
- software: PDF editor, office suite, antivirus, IDE, operating system
- subscriptions: monthly / yearly plan, support plan, cloud storage, license seats
- shopping flows: catalog, cart, wishlist, inventory, warehouse, order, discount, refund

Use this domain to make Python examples practical (e.g. product IDs, category tags, cart validation, duplicate imports, subscription feature checks).

