## Workflow (always run)

From the directory containing `mkdocs.yml` (`javascript/`):

```bash
mkdocs build --strict
```

Fix broken internal links and missing nav targets before finishing. Use `mkdocs serve` when the user wants a live preview.

When a new Python topic is added or the user asks to always update this rule, update this rule near the end of the docs work so the topic list, reference filename guidance, and coverage checklist stay current.

## Cross-links

- Link concept pages to related programs (e.g. strings core concepts → string reverse program).
- Prefer relative paths: `[Palindrome](palindrome.md)` from the same folder, or `../strings/core-concepts.md` from a sibling category.
- Do not duplicate full explanations; link to the concept page instead.

## Default problem set (when user does not specify)

Prioritize classic interview asks:

- Reverse a string (with and without `[::-1]`)
- Palindrome check (string and number)
- Find second largest in a list
- Remove duplicates, count frequency, anagram check
- Two sum, valid parentheses, merge two sorted lists (LeetCode-style)
- FizzBuzz, Fibonacci, factorial (warm-ups)

Ask before inventing a new top-level category name if an existing folder already fits.
